An interesting situation arose in my last game and did me in.  After a nasty
battle with a dwarf lord, bunches of Mordor orcs, and a couple of hill orcs
sprinkled on the side, I was a bit low on Hp's when I came upon a lowly
floating eye.  No problem, I thought.  I 'a'pplied an uncursed mirror and
got the usual message, "The floating eye is frozen by its gaze."  I changed
weapons from Stormbringer the broadsword to Grimtooth the dagger, hoping to
get a corpse out of the fight.  I hit the floating eye and got the message,
"You are frozen by the floating eye's gaze."  What gives?  Isn't the thing
frozen there?  I have done this many times before with the result being the
eye sitting there and taking the beating, often for multiple hits.  Did I just
get lucky all those other times with the eye not hitting me, or is there some-
thing different about attacking an eye with an artifact?  


[aside...]

	I lost an 11th level Valkerie on Dlvl 13 by this floating eye
problem.  I was low on Hp's after a long battle, and a tiger came up and
munched away on a tasty little Valkerie-popsicle frozen in the middle of the
room.  I didn't have a good AC (only -3) due to a scarcity of any good armour
at all.  I did get Stormbringer upon my _first_ sacrifice at my god's altar,
which I just found, i.e., not consecrated.  And, believe it or not, this one
monster sacrificed was an iguana, or some piddly little creature like that.
There has been some talk about alignments, gods, and artifacts recently, so
I thought I'd just bring up that experience.


